#  syntax: [instance].sink|source.[name].[options]=[value]
#
#  This template shows how to surface the Streaming Shuffle subsystem's metrics
#  through Spark's existing metrics system. It is a TEMPLATE: every real entry
#  below is commented out, so this file activates nothing by default. To use it,
#  copy the relevant lines into the file referenced by spark.metrics.conf
#  (for example $SPARK_HOME/conf/metrics.properties) and uncomment them.
#
#  Streaming shuffle runs on executors and is opt-in: it engages only when BOTH
#    spark.shuffle.manager=streaming  AND  spark.shuffle.streaming.enabled=true
#  Otherwise the default sort-based shuffle is used and these metrics are absent.
#
#  Source (auto-registered; no configuration line required):
#    When streaming shuffle is active, StreamingShuffleManager programmatically
#    registers a metrics source named "streamingShuffle" with the executor
#    MetricsSystem. You do NOT need an "*.source.*.class" entry for it. Its four
#    metrics are published under the "shuffle.streaming." namespace:
#
#      shuffle.streaming.bufferUtilizationPercent   (gauge)   - current buffer fill level (percent)
#      shuffle.streaming.spillCount                 (counter) - number of disk spill events
#      shuffle.streaming.backpressureEvents         (counter) - number of backpressure activations
#      shuffle.streaming.partialReadInvalidations   (counter) - partial reads invalidated on producer failure
#
#    The corresponding JMX ObjectName follows Spark's standard convention:
#      metrics:name=<application-id>.<executor-id>.streamingShuffle.shuffle.streaming.<metric>
#
#  Sinks (reused; no new dependencies). All examples below are scoped to the
#  "executor" instance and are commented out by default.
#
#  Enable the JMX sink on executors (inspect via JConsole / VisualVM):
#executor.sink.jmx.class=org.apache.spark.metrics.sink.JmxSink
#
#  Enable the Prometheus servlet sink on executors (scrape /metrics/prometheus):
#executor.sink.prometheusServlet.class=org.apache.spark.metrics.sink.PrometheusServlet
#executor.sink.prometheusServlet.path=/metrics/prometheus
#
#  Enable the CSV sink on executors:
#executor.sink.csv.class=org.apache.spark.metrics.sink.CsvSink
#executor.sink.csv.period=10
#executor.sink.csv.unit=seconds
#executor.sink.csv.directory=/tmp/spark-streaming-shuffle-metrics
#
#  Enable the Slf4j sink on executors:
#executor.sink.slf4j.class=org.apache.spark.metrics.sink.Slf4jSink
#executor.sink.slf4j.period=10
#executor.sink.slf4j.unit=seconds
